## Going-forward rules (index)

Each rule = one-line trigger + canonical-doc pointer. Body (Why / How / worked examples / sisters) lives in the canonical doc.

### Code & design

- **Structural fix preferred when bug class can recur** (2026-05-09) — `structural-fix-preferred-decision-framework.md`. Same pattern at ≥2 sites drifted apart → registry/helper-extract + compile-time enforcement.
- **Framework discipline over ad-hoc when recurrence foreseeable** (2026-05-14) — `pattern-codification-lifecycle.md`. ≥2 future applications + bug class can recur + framework cost ≤ savings×N → invest upfront.
- **Framework-driven CLI binary Stage 4 deferred to v5.16+ FOREACH_CLI_MODE** (2026-05-27) — `framework-driven-cli-binary-pattern.md`; TECH_DEBT-034. Any plan proposing framework-driven CLI binary at v5.15 → DON'T; defer to v5.16+ decoupling.
- **Deterministic skill-tool integration over LLM-orchestrated** (2026-05-28) — `structural-enforcement-when-memory-insufficient.md` (M7). Any SKILL.md amendment invoking a CI tool → EXPLICIT `python3 tools/<name>.py` in skill body, not LLM discovery.
- **Boundary-stable refactors over wide cascades** (2026-05-06) — `feedback_reduce_touch_sites.md`. Refactor crosses ≥4 files → propose stable boundary first.
- **Cohort-audit when new cfg field has 2+ siblings** (2026-05-11) — `cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md`. New boolean cfg field + 2+ semantic siblings → audit cohort.
- **Categorical applicability for new cfg fields** (2026-05-14) — `categorical-tag-applicability-pattern.md`. New cfg field → fill applies_to_* columns; no hardcoded enum names in gating.
- **Cross-file cfg surfaces use `lives_in_struct`** (2026-05-14) — same doc § Cross-file. Cfg field in non-default cfg file → tag with `lives_in_struct`.
- **Bitmap overflow static_assert mandatory** (2026-05-14) — `bitmap-overflow-protection-discipline.md`. Any FOREACH_X-paired bitmap field → co-located `static_assert(COUNT <= sizeof(type)*8)`.
- **Type-trait dispatch via `tt::` for typed registry dispatchers** (2026-05-14) — `CLAUDE.md H13`; `type-trait-dispatch-via-tt-namespace.md`. Registry-driven dispatcher → `tt::<verb>_field<T>`; never `reinterpret_cast` punning.
- **Multi-bit state encoding for K-state fields (K=2..16)** (2026-05-13) — `multi-bit-state-encoding-pattern.md`. New K-state field → N-bit packed slot + branchless inference API.
- **Cfg↔ML surface-alignment audit at every ML feature add** (2026-05-14) — RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS Class 24. New ML capability → answer 4 columns (cfg parse / Settings / Stamp / per-node override); fire `/ml-audit` at close.
- **Decision-time data binding for per-instance cfg values** (2026-05-15) — `decision-time-data-binding-pattern.md`; Class 27. Subsystem needs cfg at per-fill/event time → pre-resolve onto in-flight object; FORBIDDEN: scalar cfg-mirror field.
- **Registries optimize for ADDING; principle+sweep for ELIMINATING** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` § 1.5. Considering new registry → ask "accumulate (registry) OR shrink (counterproductive)?"
- **Branchless dispatch for SP/HP data-dependent code** (2026-05-15) — `branchless-dispatch-discipline.md`; Class 28. Data-dependent dispatch on SP/HP/drainer/producer → fn-pointer table / 2D table / pre-resolve (mispredict 30-100ns).
- **Audit hand-waves when "branch is fine" surfaces** (2026-05-15) — same doc § hand-wave. "Predictor handles it" / "only 5-15ns" → STOP; re-examine via determinism + p99.
- **Audit invocations specify scope** (2026-05-15) — `audit-scope-taxonomy.md`. Invoking audit skill → specify scope (current/wide/scoped/module/chain); default current.
- **Multi-state dispatch with per-state metadata** (2026-05-16) — `multi-state-dispatch-with-per-state-update-metadata.md`. Dispatch enum ≥3 states + behavior splits ≥2 axes → encode in X-macro row metadata.
- **Audit canonical sister before new framework infra** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_audit_canonical_sister_before_new_infra.md`; `canonical-sister-extension-discipline.md`. New registry/bit/dispatch/sidecar/macro → grep for sisters first; ≥50% overlap → EXTEND.
- **Framework-layer payoff has diminishing returns** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_framework_layer_payoff_diminishing_returns.md`. Tempted to add framework layer past inflection → recognize sites-added-vs-eliminated; stop.
- **Proportionate response to audit findings** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_proportionate_response_to_audit_findings.md`. Audit catches structural issue → full menu (INLINE/ACCEPT/FOLD/ARCHITECT); pick what's right, not first-sufficient.
- **Plan right, not fast** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_plan_right_not_fast.md`. Planning-grade decision → planning IS the hard part; decide-rightly not -quickly; indecisiveness is a feature.
- **4-pillar self-audit before surfacing recommendations** — `feedback_audit_own_proposals_with_same_rigor.md`. Before any recommendation → DESIGN_SPECS / anti-pattern / operator-impact / novel-alternative; `/readiness` Checks 31-33.
- **Future-headache vs optimization scope framework** — `feedback_future_headache_vs_optimization_scope_framework.md`. Scope discoveries during refactor → anti-pattern instance = close at ship; pure perf = defer+document.
- **Iteration spiral as audit-meta-gap signal** — `feedback_iteration_spiral_signals_audit_meta_gap.md`. Amendments finding smaller findings across 4+ cycles → STOP; codify META-gap per § 11.5; verify inflection.
- **Comprehensive consumer enumeration before registry-row deletion** — `feedback_enumerate_consumers_before_registry_row_deletion.md`. Registry row deletion/rename/source-name change → ONE comprehensive grep across all file types before plan lock.
- **Implementation-detail audit layer (M4) above SHAPE** — `feedback_implementation_detail_blindspot_recovery_via_taxonomy.md`. SHAPE audits GREEN/YELLOW after 3+ iterations OR struct-gen/type-unification/cross-registry/macro-hoist/wire-order change → fire `/blindspot-scan`.
- **Framework-driven CLI binary for cross-tool wire-format (≥3 recurrence)** (2026-05-18) — `framework-driven-cli-binary-pattern.md`. Cross-tool `tools/*.sh` mirrors engine wire-format emit + ≥3 sync events → thin C++ CLI calling engine API (no mirror).
- **B-Plus CI tool — compile-time plan body symbol verification** (2026-05-26) — `tools/check_plan_body_symbol_existence.py` + pre-commit hook + `/readiness` Check 32. Any plan body .md edit (auto at commit). Bypass `SKIP_PLAN_BODY_CHECK=1` sparingly.
- **`/capture-audit` — mechanical decision-capture drift check** (2026-05-26) — pre-commit (via `/sync-workspace`) + pre-handoff (via `/handoff`) + standalone. 11 checks; exit 0 clean / 1 findings; `--strict` blocks.
- **Session decision log discipline** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_session_decision_log_discipline.md`. Planning cycle >3 amendments OR multi-session → per-version decision log + `<!-- D/C/F -->` + `<!-- STATUS -->` sentinels; `/capture-audit` Check 3+4 enforce.
- **`/accept-handoff` — receiver-side handoff verification** (2026-05-26) — fresh-session ONE command: load handoff + cited reads + `/capture-audit --deep` + `/readiness` + recreate TaskList + verify git state + PICKUP-READY. Sister to `/handoff`.
- **Sprint sequencing — features first, then cleanup** (2026-05-26). Sprint mixing features + cleanup → features in primary sprint; cleanup gets its own dedicated ship.
- **Multi-surface deletion ordering (B14)** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_multi_surface_deletion_ordering_discipline.md`; B14 pillar. Deletion spanning ≥3 files with compile interdeps → enumerate + classify per deletion-kind + leaves-first sequence (cfg-field-row last); `/readiness` Check 41.
- **Unconditionalization latent assumption shift (B15)** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_unconditionalization_latent_assumption_audit.md`; B15 pillar. Removing cfg-gate via "always-true" → enumerate latent per-arch/per-mode assumptions; verify none load-bearing before unconditionalizing; Check 42.
- **Operator-facing doc cohort at cfg deletion** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_operator_facing_doc_cohort_at_cfg_deletion.md`. Cfg/feature deletion → sweep README + QUICKSTART + cfg.example + sister operator-docs in deletion cohort; Check 43.
- **Archived changelog preservation** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_archived_changelog_preservation_discipline.md`. Deletion/refactor touching `DOCS/changelogs/<old>` OR archived CHANGELOG rows → DO NOT modify; only current CHANGELOG gets new row at ship close.
- **Deletion-scope classification at plan-draft time** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_multi_surface_deletion_ordering_discipline.md`. Plan proposes deletion → classify SINGLE-FILE / CROSS-FILE / CROSS-SURFACE-WITH-DOCS → drives which audit fires.
- **Cfg field categorization at registry add time** (2026-05-27) — `cfg-field-categorization-discipline.md`; `/readiness` Check 44. New cfg field / re-categorization → 4-category decision tree by CONSUMER pattern (not field name); re-categorization is 5-step atomic migration.
- **C++17 inline-variable for header-only shared state** (2026-05-27) — `cpp17-inline-variable-for-header-shared-state.md`. Header-only global needing shared storage across TUs → `inline` (never `static` = per-TU copies; never extern+cpp).
- **Single source of truth discipline** (2026-05-27) — `single-source-of-truth-discipline.md`. Any fact/constant/struct/fn-body in 2+ places → MERGE unless semantic distinction (then document why).
- **Count code-LOC not total-lines for thresholds** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_count_code_loc_not_total_lines.md`. File-size/function-length/complexity check → count code-LOC (`grep -vE '^\s*(//|\*|/\*|$)'`), exclude comments+blanks.
- **Forward-decl at GLOBAL scope not inside namespace tt** (2026-05-27) — Class 34; B17 pillar. Header extraction declaring forward-decls → `namespace tt { class X; }` shadows ::X; place at global scope OR `#include`.
- **Block-scope statics need explicit-arg passing when hoisting** (2026-05-27) — Class 35; B18 pillar. Lambda/fn hoist into different scope → enumerate enclosing block-scope statics; pass each as explicit arg.
- **Sister-cohort amendment completeness** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_sister_cohort_amendment_completeness.md`. Any Class/DESIGN_SPEC/ledger amendment → enumerate sister-cohort (cross-refs + reverse cross-refs); parallel-amend same ship; `/capture-audit` Check 9.
- **Forward-promise auto-write verification at next-ship** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_forward_promise_auto_write_verification.md`; `/capture-audit` Check 11. Ship-close/handoff/next-ship-pickup → verify prior forward-promises landed at expected ledger; surface unfulfilled.
- **Test change enumeration per plan body** (2026-05-28) — `feedback_test_change_enumeration_per_plan_body.md`; `/readiness` Check 45. Plan body modifying engine `tests/` → dedicated "Tests changed" section (modified / broken-replaced / NEW).
- **Proactive rename candidate surfacing** (2026-05-28) — `feedback_proactive_rename_candidate_surfacing.md`; running list. Throughout multi-ship restructures → FLAG renames as encountered; classify 4-tier; scan list at each planning gate.
- **Terminology-evolution bridge, not history rewrite** (2026-05-28) — `feedback_terminology_evolution_bridge_not_history_rewrite.md`; DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY § 15 Glossary; Class 36. Architecture-wide rename → SWEEP forward-looking docs; PRESERVE historical-record; BRIDGE via glossary; code symbols defer to code-rename ship.
- **Prose-token rename tools unsafe for code/transition-PLANNING docs (B19)** (2026-05-28) — B19 pillar; TECH_DEBT-142; Class 36. Code rename OR docs that *describe* a rename → AST/symbol-aware tooling, not prose-token (over-renames citations / current-state / transition-context).
- **Golden-master over reimplemented oracle** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_golden_master_over_reimplemented_oracle.md`. Validating a path → freeze its REAL output + diff (golden-master/characterization); NEVER reimplement/stub an oracle (Class-18 mirror that drifts + lies). Lowest drift/failure risk; standing CI gate. Sister: single-source-of-truth + Class 18.
- **Phased pre-rework correctness foundation + net-gating scoping** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_phased_pre_rework_correctness_foundation.md`; D-73. High-risk multi-ship restructure → phase the foundation (bedrock→lock-current→root-GREEN→sweep→gate); the no-reintroduction guarantee is the NET (CI/tests on current codebase) not audits; minimal pre-rework scope = net-gating findings only (what the net is meaningless without).
- **Enumerate the set before a categorical risk-dismissal** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_enumerate_set_before_categorical_claim.md`. Dismissing a risk / bounding scope via "the rest are [property]" → enumerate the set's members + verify each + name any non-conformer. Class-33 enumeration lifted to the risk-assessment/self-audit layer (`.E.0.1` R1 instance: FromDouble assumed exact-integer; wasn't).
- **Heavier-default audit posture for capital** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_heavier_default_audit_posture_for_capital.md`; D-77; `/precoding-audit-gate` "Audit posture" §. Money-bearing code → default the HEAVIER audit/pre-coding pass; LIGHT is EARNED only where a Tier-1/2 deterministic guard already covers the surface (weight ∝ inverse deterministic coverage; read off the guard-coverage-matrix). Empirical: 141 `.E.0` findings from light-pass-audited code.
- **Independent deliverable-review at session close** (2026-05-29) — `/close-session` Stage 5.5; D-79. Substantial multi-artifact close → spawn an INDEPENDENT reviewer (anti-self-attestation; the builder shouldn't attest its own work) verifying deliverables landed complete + coherent across 6 dimensions (landed / coherent+propagated / no-fabrication / edits-surgical+WH-2 / acceptance-criteria / privacy-boundary); skip trivial. Sister: `/precoding-audit-gate` Stage 3.5.
- **Meta-anti-pattern catalog — the META parallel of RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS** (2026-05-29) — `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/meta-anti-pattern-index.md`; D-75/D-76. Recurring NON-code error (audit-reasoning / planning / workspace-hygiene / cascade) → catalog it (an INDEX of M1-M7 + B14-B19 + feedback; populated by the `/close-session` harvest; consumed by `/capture-audit` Check 12 + the hardened gate).
- **Independence is for judgment, not mechanical checks** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_independence_for_judgment_not_mechanical.md`. Designing a check/skill-stage → mechanical detection runs the TOOL directly (determinism = independence; agent = overhead); judgment-on-own-work runs an INDEPENDENT agent (anti-self-attestation); mechanizing a judgment-check eliminates its agent. Run the leanest executor.
- **Skill-edit cohort checklist** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_skill_edit_cohort_checklist.md`. Editing a SKILL.md → run the checklist (own cross-ref section / frontmatter loads_dynamically+sister_specs both-ways / CLAUDE.md skill suite if NEW / catalog both-ways / `check_doc_metadata --bidirectional`); sister-cohort-completeness specialized to skills; mechanical half folds into #14.
- **Never skip thoroughness unless explicitly stated** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_never_skip_thoroughness_unless_explicit.md`; catalog PL-2. Thorough steps (independent review / audit gate / blindspot / readiness check) fire BY DEFAULT; the agent does NOT self-skip on "redundant/trivial/already-covered"; skip is operator-EXPLICIT only (flag / stated "skip it"); a review fires on UN-reviewed work regardless of prior passes on other work. Skills' "When to skip" = operator-discretion, not agent-discretion (skill-sweep pending, #15). Extends heavier-default (D-77) from audit-depth → step-skipping.
- **Runtime executor mode {independent|self|both} for judgment skills** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_runtime_executor_mode_for_judgment_skills.md`. Judgment/audit skills take a per-invocation `executor` arg: `independent` (default, spawn fresh agent — anti-self-attestation) / `self` (inline, cheaper, operator-EXPLICIT) / `both` (run+compare, max rigor/calibration). Operator defers the independence call at runtime; mechanical skills ignore it. Default independent. Wired across skills via #15; canonical instance `/close-session` Stage 5.5.
- **Close the class structurally ≠ migrate every site** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_close_the_class_vs_migrate_every_site.md`; D-84. Recurring bug class across many sites → close it via the primitive + an enforcing CI guard (new violations = build error; existing KNOWN-PENDING + shrinking); the guard de-risks paced site-migration, so "close the class" ≠ "migrate everything now". Specializes structural-fix; dissolves the do-it-all-now-vs-defer-to-later-sweep dichotomy.
- **Two foundations: determinism vs correctness** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_two_foundations_determinism_vs_correctness.md`; D-82. Reproducibility (net-gating; freeze CURRENT deterministic behavior) and exact-values (deliberate, regen the golden) are orthogonal axes; a pre-rework net freezes current behavior, correctness fixes are separate deliberate changes; don't let "make it exact first" block the determinism net.
- **Guard-matrix bounds foundation-hardening** (2026-05-29) — `feedback_guard_matrix_bounds_foundation_hardening.md`; D-83. The guard-coverage-matrix is the STOP condition for "make it solid first": harden until every invariant the next phase touches is an enforced row (no HOLE/TBD), then build; turns "solid enough" into a checklist; sister to D-73 + heavier-default (D-77).

### Thread isolation between subsystems

- **GUI ↔ HP/SP thread isolation: NEVER share state directly** (2026-05-14) — `universal-registry-bitmap-dispatcher-pattern.md` § GUI↔engine. Subsystem touching engine state cross-thread → typed mirror per side + file + reload-signal; never pointer-share (H3).

### Process & sprint

- **Plan body length has NO target LOC** (2026-05-28) — `feedback_plan_body_length_no_target_loc.md`. Drafting/assessing plan → as much detail as needed; never cite "under 1200"; assess by completeness. (Always-loaded 600 + tests 5K keep thresholds.)
- **Audit re-fire at substantive plan amendment** (2026-05-27) — `/precoding-audit-gate` re-fire on architectural-shift / scope-reframe / categorization-change / framework-pattern-question. Sister to iteration-spiral + pushback-as-signal.
- **Suggest mid-sprint audits when work impacts downstream** (2026-05-10). HIGH-RISK ship / first pattern application / cross-cutting → suggest `/test-strength-audit` + `/dod-audit` + `/parity-check`; await greenlight.
- **Sub-plan sidecar files for substantial code-sample sections** (2026-05-16) — `<plan-name>-examples.md`. Section >100 LOC OR multi-file coordination OR new framework pattern → sidecar.
- **Each DESIGN_SPECS doc has a CLAUDE.md cross-ref** (2026-05-09). Format: `Pattern documented in DESIGN_SPECS/<name>.md.` at end of relevant item.
- **Codify design principles in CLAUDE.md as patterns mature** (2026-05-09). Promote once: ≥2 applications OR DESIGN_SPECS doc exists, AND pattern is broad.
- **Auto-pick the more future-oriented option when trade-off clear** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_auto_pick_future_oriented.md`. Surface ONLY when future-vs-now sharp OR genuinely ambiguous; never punt auto-decidable.
- **Audit → update → implement → ship cycle PER sub-ship** (2026-05-17). Each sub-ship → `/precoding-audit-gate` → triage + consult → update plan → implement → ship + postmortem.
- **Plans introducing new registries cite sister inspection** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_plans_cite_sister_registry_inspection.md`; `/readiness` Check 29. Plan proposes new registry/bit/dispatch → "Canonical sister registries considered" section.
- **Anti-spaghetti audit on cadence** (2026-05-17) — `project_anti_spaghetti_audit_cadence.md`. Quarterly + post-new-anti-pattern sweep + ad-hoc.
- **New plans use future-oriented plan template** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_new_plans_use_future_oriented_template.md`; `future-oriented-plan-template.md`.
- **Plans + sub-plans codify explicit end goals** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_plans_have_explicit_end_goal.md`; plan templates. Drafting MASTER/sub-plan/handoff → "end goal" + acceptance criteria + MASTER tie-back.

### Docs & files

- **New docs default to private** (2026-05-06). Doc captures unshipped direction / optimization / operator-edge → `plans/`. Public architectural-only → `DOCS/`. Auto-private: `*_AUDIT.md`, `FUTURE_*.md`, `*-design-notes.md`, `*.local.md`, etc.
- **Workspace mirror for edge content** (2026-05-06) — `/sync-workspace` canonical. Mirrors plans/, skills (symlink); cfgs/.env/*.local.md (copy).
- **Cold-pickup plan completeness — 10 fields** (2026-05-06) — `/readiness` Cold-pickup section canonical.
- **Long-term doc-system evolution visions at `plans/_future/`** (2026-05-28) — (a) `2026-05-28-docs-as-meta-code-roadmap.md`; (b) `2026-05-28-context-aware-claude-md-loading-roadmap.md`. Trigger: v6.X+ post-decoupling OR CLAUDE.md >1200 lines OR multi-language scale.
- **Doc layer separation: always-loaded vs on-demand** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do.md`; CLAUDE.md § Doc layer separation. Editing CLAUDE.md/local/MEMORY/SKILL → TIMELESS guidelines+triggers+pointers only; sprint TODO → TECH_DEBT/plans.
- **Categorical triggers > hardcoded refs in always-loaded content** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_categorical_triggers_over_hardcoded_refs.md`; `categorical-triggers-in-always-loaded-docs.md`. Always-loaded trigger → categorical patterns, not hardcoded fn/TECH_DEBT-NNN/path. Stable catalog IDs (Class/H/M N) keep.
- **Universal YAML frontmatter for cross-referenced docs** (2026-05-18) — `doc-frontmatter-convention.md`; `doc-tag-vocabulary.md`. Doc >50 lines OR cross-referenced → frontmatter (type/stage/version/tags/surface/sister_specs).
- **Quarterly /metadata-audit cadence** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_metadata_audit_quarterly.md`. Quarterly + post-codification + operator-flagged.
- **File-size split discipline** (2026-05-18; RESCOPED 2026-05-27) — `file-size-split-discipline.md` v1.4. SELECTIVE in AI-solo workflow: always-loaded docs 600 + tests 5K RETAINED; source/header/plan/SKILL/DESIGN_SPECS thresholds → guidelines.
- **Registry default = SSoT for cfg defaults** (2026-05-19) — `universal-cfg-field-registry-pattern.md` § Registry-default precedence. New cfg field with registry default → manual struct initializer FORBIDDEN; per-row resolution at sweep (MATCH delete / DIFFER operator-decide).
- **Memories are structured doc-system citizens** (2026-05-30) — `doc-frontmatter-convention.md` § memory/*.md (Stage 3); D-89. NEW memories use `/doc-create memory` (or the canonical schema directly: harness-native `name`/`description`/`metadata.type` PRESERVED + `metadata.tags` from `doc-tag-vocabulary` + unified `metadata.sister_specs`, nested under `metadata:`). Covered by `check_doc_metadata --bidirectional --memories` (one-way sister = red build; `/capture-audit` Check 12); `tools/migrate_memory_frontmatter.py` re-derives + symmetrizes sisters from body `[[links]]` at `/sync-workspace`. NEVER hand-write a bare old-format (no-tags) memory.

### Operator collaboration

- **Address Caramel as Caramel / she / her** (`feedback_address_user_as_caramel.md`).
- **No AskUserQuestion modal boxes** — inline options (`feedback_no_question_boxes.md`).
- **Evaluate options on robustness + latency + design philosophy, NOT time** (`feedback_evaluate_options_on_robustness_latency_design_not_time.md`).
- **After pre-coding checks, ALWAYS consult before coding** (`feedback_consult_on_audit_findings.md`).
- **Sequential per-target audits for granular triage** (2026-05-28) — `feedback_sequential_audit_for_granular_operator_triage.md`. Multi-target audit batch (>5) → sequential per-target when correctness>speed; hybrid = codebase-wide parallel → per-target sequential.
- **Defer is last-ditch, never effort-avoidance** (`feedback_no_defer_for_effort.md`).
- **Compaction degrades — verify handoffs against current code** (`feedback_compaction_degrades_treat_handoffs_as_hints.md`).
- **Motivated collaborator for Caramel** (`feedback_motivated_collaborator_for_caramel.md`). Public AGPL + hedge-fund attention → pick best-software path even when costlier now.
- **Backwards compat NOT a default concern** (2026-05-26; REFINED) — `feedback_backwards_compat_not_default_concern.md`. Refactor/deletion → cleanest answer (no preserve-and-deprecate) unless operator flags load-bearing exception (stamp body / persistence / model handle / locked cfg). Operator-migration-impact SECTION still required (SECTION ≠ PATH).

